      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. this look good. can you expand on the section about \"external interference\" and \"security risks\" during transit? specifically, i want to cover what the staff should do if they notice something is off—like if a container looks like it's been meddled with or if there's any sign of unauthorized people hanging around the shipment at a transit hub. what are the standard steps to figure out if a breach was just an accident or if someone was actually trying to intercept the cargo? i need to know how to distinguish between a simple mishap and a deliberate attempt at theft or tampering.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
